{"name":"Chestnut Stallion","hex":"#995d3b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chestnut","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edible nut (technically a fruit) of the Spanish chestnut or sweet chestnut tree (Castanea sativa); also (chiefly preceded by a descriptive word), a nut from a related shrub or tree; or a similar nut from an unrelated plant.","In full chestnut tree: the shrub or tree that bears this nut, the Spanish chestnut or sweet chestnut (Castanea sativa); also (chiefly preceded by a descriptive word), a shrub or tree of the genus Castanea."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a deep reddish-brown colour, like that of a chestnut fruit (noun sense 1)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chestnut"},{"term":"stallion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An adult male horse.\nSpecifically, one that is uncastrated.\nA male horse kept primarily as a stud.","Specifically, one that is uncastrated."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stallion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chestnut","blocks":[{"text":"Chestnuts are the deciduous trees and shrubs in the genus Castanea, in the beech family Fagaceae. The name also refers to the edible nuts they produce. They are native to temperate regions of the Northern Hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Ch%C3%A2taignier_120807_1.jpg/330px-Ch%C3%A2taignier_120807_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chestnut","wikidata":"Q129324"},{"title":"Stallion","blocks":[{"text":"A stallion is an adult male horse that has not been gelded (castrated). Stallions follow the conformation and phenotype of their breed, but within that standard, the presence of hormones such as testosterone may give stallions a thicker, \"cresty\" neck, as well as a somewhat more muscular physique as compared to female horses, known as mares, and castrated males, called geldings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Puerto_rican-Paso-Fino-Horse-chestnut.jpg/330px-Puerto_rican-Paso-Fino-Horse-chestnut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stallion","wikidata":"Q757833"},{"title":"Chestnut (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Chestnut or castaneous is a colour, a medium reddish shade of brown, and is named after the nut of the chestnut tree. An alternate name for the colour is badious."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chestnut_(color)","wikidata":"Q2040833"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Chestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG/500px-Chestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Chestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG/1280px-Chestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Chestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG/500px-Chestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Sweet_chestnut_DSCF0160.JPG/500px-Sweet_chestnut_DSCF0160.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Sweet_chestnut_DSCF0160.JPG/1280px-Sweet_chestnut_DSCF0160.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Sweet_chestnut_DSCF0160.JPG/500px-Sweet_chestnut_DSCF0160.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bark of C. sativa